-- (3) Linearity giving the safety test, as far as reasoned: a wire has two ends, the one a value
-- is delivered at and the one an operation is placed at. A plan delivers values only at ends its
-- pair holds (an operation's out wires, a duplicate's two wires) or at new wires, places operations
-- only at ends its pair holds (the argument, the wires of the value's parts) or at new wires, and
-- sets only its own wire. A memory is linear when each end of each wire is held by at most one
-- cell; references are the exception, any number may name a held wire, and a held wire is written
-- once. Then for two different pairs every two changes are on different wires or are the two ends
